WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
When 18-year-old Rhea saw this influencer's post, it felt familiar.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.040
That's because it was her selfie video.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.080
But it had been digitally altered to have much darker skin

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.520
and had been posted by an account posing as a black influencer.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.260
The account was made in December and gained 3 million followers within just a few weeks.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.600
What happened to Rhea is only the surface of what we found.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.820
We've been investigating dozens of fake AI influencer pages on Instagram and TikTok

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.340
which sexualized and stereotyped black women.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:32.040
They use AI-generated images of black women that do not exist.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.340
The profiles follow normal influencers' online behavior,

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.520
viral dances, lip syncs to trending music, and short lifestyle clips.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.860
But there's a pattern too.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.240
They often show black women dressed in skimpy swimwear or other revealing clothing,

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:50.620
portrayed with exaggerated body shapes, and digitally imposed extremely dark skin tones.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.520
Account names often include terms such as black, noir, dark, and ebony.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.140
A few of the accounts include comments about white men in their posts.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.960
Many of the accounts follow or like each other's posts.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:10.400
There is a racist theme here, so I think it does cater to people who are into racist themes.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.520
This is a race fetish account, that's what this is, and there are a lot of others,

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.160
so we can see that this is a trend.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.600
And the person in this case is AI-generated, there are no consequences for them.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.420
What's happening away from Instagram and TikTok is concerning too.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:36.220
We collaborated with AI researcher Jeremy Carrasco and his team and found that at least 60 of these accounts linked to paid for sexually explicit content on third party sites.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:46.020
I think that they're probably making pretty decent money because some of these third party sites have, they have a lot of followers and the subscriptions aren't exactly cheap.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:51.680
So I think that the incentives are pretty good right now, even if it's really unethical to do.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:56.100
On those external sites, the avatars are labeled as AI-generated.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.520
But on Instagram and TikTok, where millions of people see them,

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.620
most accounts don't disclose their AI at all.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.740
In apparent breach of the platform's guidelines,

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.120
some of these accounts even deny that they're not real when asked by followers.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.420
The person who's on camera doesn't have any shame.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.680
They're AI-generated.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.900
There's no real person standing up and saying,

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.600
this isn't okay, I won't participate in this.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.280
So it is a thing that AI uniquely exploits.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.360
Moroccan model and content creator Huda,

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:27.800
who advocates for more authentic representations of black women,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.940
says this trend is about erasure.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:53.200
We identified dozens of accounts with these features across Instagram and TikTok.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.500
This one, which used Model Rhea's content, was one of the biggest pages.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:03.640
Some videos have hundreds of millions of views and the comments are flooded with praise and compliments.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.620
They didn't change anything else but my appearance.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.760
So it's still my house. It's still my emotions.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.280
Rhea says she reported the account multiple times on Instagram and TikTok.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.680
But at the time, the videos remained online.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:24.040
One manipulated clip received tens of millions of views, far more than the original video she posted herself.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:36.480
Actually, I'm not sure if I'm more concerned about them taking my video to promote their explicit content or people actually believe in that and falling for this.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:44.460
After the BBC contacted TikTok with the examples of the accounts we found, the company said it had removed content and banned accounts that broke its rules.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:50.040
Within a few days, 20 accounts had been labeled banned on the app, including the one that used Ria's content.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:55.320
TikTok says it prohibits AI-generated content that uses someone's likeness without permission

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:58.820
and requires creators to label realistic AI content.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:04.500
Instagram's parent company, Meta, says it's investigating the accounts identified by the BBC.
